| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 0 | 5 | abanan | n | false |
| 1 | 3 | anaban | n | false |
| 2 | 1 | ananab | b | false |
| 3 | 0 | banana | a | true |
| 4 | 4 | nabana | a | false |
| 5 | 2 | nanaba | a | false |

Actual sorted starts: [5, 3, 1, 0, 4, 2]. Inverse: banana.
\image(figures/bwt_rotations.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The green row is the original string. The displayed matrix is constructed only for this tiny diagram; the core sorter keeps start indices and does not allocate an n-by-n byte matrix.)
\alttext(Six sorted rotations are abanan, anaban, ananab, banana, nabana and nanaba. Their last bytes are n, n, b, a, a and a. Banana is highlighted at row three.)

The pair is (L,I)=(nnbaaa,3). Each last-column position comes from exactly
one rotation start, so L is a permutation of the input bytes. Length and
symbol frequencies are unchanged. The primary row is necessary because
cyclic rotations share a last column; it selects which rotation to recover.
Equal rotations are tied by increasing start offset, giving deterministic
results and selecting the first row equal to the input.

The original [Burrows and Wheeler report](https://www.cs.jhu.edu/~langmea/resources/burrows_wheeler.pdf)
describes this cyclic, primary-index convention. The library uses the same
byte ordering in both directions, including zero and high-bit bytes. The
previous forward comparator used signed char order on this platform while
the inverse used unsigned order, breaking some binary round trips.

> Stable occurrences define the LF mapping

The first column F is the sorted multiset of L. For a byte c, let C[c]
count bytes strictly below c, and let rank(i) count earlier occurrences of
L[i] in L, starting at zero. The native mapping is

\[
LF(i)=C[L[i]]+\operatorname{rank}(i).
\]

This pairs each occurrence in L with the same occurrence in F. Within a
fixed byte group, moving the last byte to the front preserves the order
of the remaining context. Thus LF identifies a cyclic predecessor row's
*content*. With duplicate rotations, its chosen row need not have the
literal predecessor's original start offset; equal row contents suffice.

Starting from I, read L at the current row, write the output from right
to left, and follow LF. Perform exactly n writes. For banana, the actual
row sequence is 3,0,4,1,5,2 and the written bytes are a,n,a,n,a,b.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bwt_lf_walk.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::bwt_inverse_trace(dm::algorithms::bwt_transform("banana"));
  std::print("| row | L byte | earlier equal occurrences | C[L] | LF(row) | F at row |\n"
             "| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (std::size_t row=0;row<trace.input.transformed.size();++row) {
    const auto value=static_cast<unsigned char>(trace.input.transformed[row]);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",row,static_cast<char>(value),trace.mapping.occurrence_rank[row],
        trace.mapping.starts[value],trace.mapping.lf[row],trace.mapping.first_column[row]);
  }
  std::print("\n| actual step | current row | read byte | output position | next LF row |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> positions{{0,0},{4.6,0},{9.2,0},{9.2,-3.4},{4.6,-3.4},{0,-3.4}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=3.7;style.height=1.8;
  for (std::size_t k=0;k<trace.steps.size();++k) {
    const auto& step=trace.steps[k];
    diagram.node(std::format("step{}",k),positions[k],std::format("row {}: L={}\nwrite output[{}]\nnext row {}",
        step.row,static_cast<char>(step.value),step.output_index,step.next_row),style);
    if (k) diagram.edge(std::format("step{}",k-1),std::format("step{}",k));
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,step.row,static_cast<char>(step.value),step.output_index,step.next_row);
  }
  diagram.text({4.6,-5.2},std::format("output: {}; filled right to left in exactly {} writes",trace.output,trace.steps.size()),18)
      .save_svg("build/bwt_lf_walk.svg");
  if (trace.output!="banana" || trace.steps.size()!=6) return 1;
  std::print("\nLF: {}. Reconstructed: {}.\n",trace.mapping.lf,trace.output);
}
